2026-09-27T09:57:28.1147743Z Update Note
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1148047Z ===========
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1148485Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1148915Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1149050Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1149362Z ================
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1149537Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1149769Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1150299Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1150630Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1150801Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1151213Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1151459Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1151661Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1152230Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1152758Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1153701Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1154519Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1154662Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1155302Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1156321Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1231553Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1232047Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1232699Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1232846Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1233178Z ========
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1233353Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1235358Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1236804Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1237067Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1237532Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1238453Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1239027Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1239570Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1239974Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1240362Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1240476Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1240715Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1240851Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1241842Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1242890Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1243488Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1244304Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:57:28.1244510Z 
